Id: php004w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_php
Fix: Set allow_url_fopen = Off in php.ini.
References: php.ini directives
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6, SI-10; ISO 8.9, 8.28; CE Secure configuration

PHP treats URLs as files: any file function an attacker reaches
fetches their server's answer. Remote code inclusion is php001w's
business; this is reads. Turn allow_url_fopen off unless the
applications fetch URLs themselves. Judged at the effective value
across php.ini and its conf.d drop-ins; the file named set it.
